Z||000014||MinnGreenGT||10-02-2001||11:38 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GTFiero1:<BR><B>has anybody ever had that dream where in the dream your falling then you wake up and the moment you wake up it acctually felt like your falling?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>When I was little (like 5 or 6) I remember falling off a cliff in my dream... and woke up a split second before hitting the ground.  I was sleeping in the top bunk of a bunk-bed without the railing (so that's why they put those on there).<P>I ocassionally dream about Fieros too... the other night I had a "hard core" dream about making a Fiero trailer from an old damaged GT. I woke up a 5am and couldn't back to sleep... just kept thinking about the trailer. So now I'm looking around for a GT Fastback sailpanel that is damaged (I don't really want to chop up a good one for this type of project... that would be almost sacreligous).||||reg||1
Z||000015||DKOV||10-02-2001||01:49 PM||||I once had a dream that my 88GT was stolen from the parking lot of a concert hall and I was walking around at night looking for it.  I went to the gas station across the street and asked the guy if he had seen it and he said that a gang of Asian Triad Gangsters had taken it and they happened to be in the building next door.  So I went in and found the car in teh middle of the floor all perfect.  There were about 50 badguys standing all around and when they noticed me, it turned into a Jackie Chan movie with me trying to make my way to the Fiero while 50 Cops poured in from every window and skylight. Sure I threw a few punches but mostly I was just trying to get to my car.  When I did, I lit up the tires and got out of there!<P>I have no idea how Jackie did after I left, but knowing him... He did just fine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DKOV -||||reg||10
